# The assessment of WORK-LEDGER-005 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the identity is
# a second place for it to be wrong — the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a record registration,
# and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# WORK-LEDGER-005 requires blocked work to classify the blocker as dependency, decision,
# territory mismatch, external resource, needs-split, stale probe artifact, or other typed
# cause rather than relying only on prose notes. `Blocker` declares six of the seven, in the
# requirement's own order. `StaleProbeArtifact` is absent, and OD-LEDGER-017 is the record:
# it decides the absence is a decline rather than an omission, on the ground that the cause
# has no referent in this build — the nearest candidate, a committed projection going stale,
# is inside the holder's own hands and so is not the kind of thing `Blocker` answers about —
# and it names the event that would reverse the decline. The requirement's list ends "or
# other typed cause" and `Blocker::Other { detail }` is declared, so every blocker this build
# can have remains expressible as a typed cause.
#
# The two sites are the transcription and the membership check. `CORPUS_CAUSES` carries the
# seven causes in the requirement's order with the declined row empty; `Corpus_Position` is
# the exhaustive match that makes a seventh variant a compile error at the table rather than
# a cause the assertions would never visit. If either goes, the decline stops being held by
# anything and this verdict is about nothing.
#
# Not recomputed from the corpus at check time. OD-TRACE-001 records why: CI has no corpus,
# so a guard that read one would be green by being unable to look.
verdict: Diverges
record: OD-LEDGER-017
site: crates/substrate/nomos-ledger/src/item/tests.rs#CORPUS_CAUSES
site: crates/substrate/nomos-ledger/src/item/tests.rs#Corpus_Position
